WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.360 --> 00:00:05.040
Antoine Fuqua and Denzel Washington&nbsp;
reunite for the final entry in "The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.040 --> 00:00:08.760
Equalizer" trilogy, bringing the&nbsp;
franchise's violent action and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:08.760 --> 00:00:13.620
captivating vigilante to a new setting.&nbsp;
So what happens to Robert McCall at the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:13.620 --> 00:00:15.600
end of "Equalizer 3"?
Serenity in Sicily?

00:00:15.600 --> 00:00:18.780
In the third film, Robert is&nbsp;
nearly on his deathbed after&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:18.780 --> 00:00:22.740
getting a bullet to the back during&nbsp;
a secret mission in Sicily. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:22.740 --> 00:00:28.897
he's saved by a local doctor named Enzo and stays&nbsp;
in a small Sicilian village while he recovers.

00:00:28.897 --> 00:00:31.980
There, Robert grows fond of the&nbsp;
village and its people -- which&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:31.980 --> 00:00:34.297
leaves him wondering if he could find peace here.

00:00:34.297 --> 00:00:39.120
Unfortunately, Robert is unable to stay out&nbsp;
of a tense situation that unfolds as a local&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:39.120 --> 00:00:44.160
crime boss named Vincent continually&nbsp;
strikes fear over the town. So Robert&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:44.160 --> 00:00:48.774
attempts to protect the people he's come&nbsp;
to love and destroy Vincent's drug empire.

00:00:48.774 --> 00:00:52.620
"The Equalizer 3" sees Robert face&nbsp;
one of his most vicious and powerful&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:52.620 --> 00:00:56.280
foes yet while dealing with his&nbsp;
own personal demons. Robert is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:56.280 --> 00:01:00.360
at his most human in the final franchise&nbsp;
installment, coming to grips with his own&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:00.360 --> 00:01:04.678
actions while also attempting to protect&nbsp;
this new community he's become a part of.

00:01:04.678 --> 00:01:08.940
Not to mention, there's plenty of brutal&nbsp;
action that'll leave audiences shaken. With&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:08.940 --> 00:01:13.800
"The Equalizer 3" likely being Washington's last&nbsp;
appearance in this franchise, let's delve into the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:13.800 --> 00:01:16.920
film's ending and see where Robert's story ends.
The final stretch

00:01:16.920 --> 00:01:21.180
Robert attempts to enlist the help&nbsp;
of a CIA agent named Emma to break&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:21.180 --> 00:01:25.380
up Vincent's empire. Unfortunately, Emma&nbsp;
ends up in the hospital due to Vincent's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:25.380 --> 00:01:30.177
corrupt power and reach being so widespread&nbsp;
-- so Robert is forced to act on his own.

00:01:30.177 --> 00:01:33.998
"Whatever it is you and your&nbsp;
friends do, do it somewhere else."

00:01:33.998 --> 00:01:35.198
"Are you warning me?"

00:01:35.257 --> 00:01:36.457
"I'm preparing."

00:01:36.457 --> 00:01:40.680
After slaying Vincent's brother Marco,&nbsp;
Vincent is furious with Robert and comes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:40.680 --> 00:01:44.820
to the village for some swift vengeance. He&nbsp;
threatens to kill the locals unless Robert&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:44.820 --> 00:01:48.598
gives himself up -- leading to Robert&nbsp;
coming out of the shadows to face him.

00:01:48.598 --> 00:01:53.640
Although Robert seems outmatched, he's joined&nbsp;
by the locals in standing against Vincent. Enzo&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:53.640 --> 00:01:57.556
shoots at Vincent while everyone else pulls&nbsp;
out their phones to record the situation.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:57.556 --> 00:02:01.500
With Vincent not wanting his actions to be&nbsp;
public, he says that this conflict between&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:01.500 --> 00:02:07.115
him and Robert isn't over, and Robert agrees&nbsp;
-- kicking off a gruesome final stretch.

00:02:07.320 --> 00:02:12.420
The tensions between Vincent and Robert reach a&nbsp;
point where a final confrontation is inevitable.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:12.420 --> 00:02:18.180
Vincent and his men are shown concocting a plan,&nbsp;
but Robert ends up striking first. He makes his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:18.180 --> 00:02:22.560
way to Vincent's mansion and picks off each of&nbsp;
Vincent's guards one by one, holding nothing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:22.560 --> 00:02:27.238
back. Eventually, Robert slaughters all of&nbsp;
Vincent's men, leaving Vincent on his own.

00:02:27.238 --> 00:02:32.760
After tying Vincent up, Robert feeds him his&nbsp;
own drugs. With Vincent's time dwindling by the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:32.760 --> 00:02:37.920
second, Robert decides to untie Vincent and let&nbsp;
him run away. Robert is with him every step of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:37.920 --> 00:02:42.360
the way, though, acting as his haunting shadow.&nbsp;
Meanwhile, the people of the village are having&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:42.360 --> 00:02:47.100
a religious procession through the streets, which&nbsp;
could possibly be interpreted as them asking for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:47.100 --> 00:02:52.678
forgiveness for Robert's actions. Or it could be a&nbsp;
sign of thanks to God for bringing Robert to them.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:52.777 --> 00:02:57.517
Either way, Robert continues to follow Vincent&nbsp;
until he's lying nearly dead in the streets.

00:02:58.020 --> 00:03:02.580
Shortly after Robert leaves Vincent for dead on&nbsp;
the streets, Emma receives congratulations for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:02.580 --> 00:03:07.680
her work in breaking up Vincent's drug operation.&nbsp;
His corrupt empire has finally been brought down,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:07.680 --> 00:03:12.120
meaning that the streets will be a little bit&nbsp;
safer. Emma even gets a visit from Robert,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:12.120 --> 00:03:15.995
who tells her why he became involved&nbsp;
in this situation in the first place.

00:03:15.995 --> 00:03:21.060
It turns out that Robert was in Sicily on his&nbsp;
own personal mission, attempting to retrieve&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:21.060 --> 00:03:25.500
stolen pension money for a man he met while&nbsp;
driving for Lyft. He never intended on getting&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:25.500 --> 00:03:30.637
involved in something bigger, nor expected to&nbsp;
find anything more sinister than petty thieves.

00:03:30.637 --> 00:03:35.040
However, this experience has made him find&nbsp;
a deeper sense of purpose that's allowed him&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:35.040 --> 00:03:39.017
to finally find some peace. There's&nbsp;
just one question remaining though:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:39.017 --> 00:03:45.605
"You don't wanna play games with me."
"Just having my tea."

00:03:45.605 --> 00:03:49.860
Well, it turns out that Emma is actually the&nbsp;
daughter of his former colleague Susan Plummer,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:49.860 --> 00:03:53.100
so Robert knew that he could&nbsp;
trust her. The boost to Emma's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:53.100 --> 00:03:56.916
career is a way for Robert to help&nbsp;
Susan's family long after her death.&nbsp;

00:03:56.916 --> 00:04:01.380
Sometime later, Emma is seen giving the pension&nbsp;
money back to the man Robert mentioned. Robert,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:01.380 --> 00:04:06.515
meanwhile, gets to reside in the community that&nbsp;
gave him purpose, putting his old life behind him.

00:04:06.840 --> 00:04:10.500
Robert has been a vengeful force&nbsp;
throughout "The Equalizer" franchise,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:10.500 --> 00:04:14.220
but his arc in this third film is&nbsp;
about his personal journey toward a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:14.220 --> 00:04:18.780
more peaceful life. Despite him still being&nbsp;
an unmatched fighter and merciless killer,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:18.780 --> 00:04:21.600
he's brought back to reality&nbsp;
when he's unexpectedly shot.

00:04:21.600 --> 00:04:25.500
Robert has rarely been so caught&nbsp;
off guard or close to death before,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:25.500 --> 00:04:31.020
and the shock of it nearly causes him to take his&nbsp;
own life. However, once Enzo starts to heal him&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:31.020 --> 00:04:36.360
and takes him into his small village, Robert&nbsp;
is given much-needed clarity and purpose. The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:36.360 --> 00:04:40.920
kindness he sees in this town legitimately leaves&nbsp;
a big impact. For the first time in a while,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:40.920 --> 00:04:46.036
he finds peace and acceptance, which allows&nbsp;
him to feel like he belongs in this place.

00:04:46.036 --> 00:04:48.900
"Because of these people, I'm&nbsp;
beginning to understand real peace."

00:04:48.900 --> 00:04:54.038
However, he's still concerned about falling&nbsp;
into old patterns when Vincent arrives.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:54.038 --> 00:04:59.318
Uncharacteristically, Robert initially stands&nbsp;
aside so as to not ruin this quaint paradise.

00:04:59.318 --> 00:05:04.020
There's an internal conflict within Robert&nbsp;
that has him questioning his purpose within&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:04.020 --> 00:05:08.340
this community and whether he can act without&nbsp;
being seen as being as a violent man like&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:08.340 --> 00:05:13.140
Vincent. Eventually, though, Robert understands&nbsp;
that acting is better than standing by while&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:13.140 --> 00:05:18.497
others he's grown to love get hurt. His action&nbsp;
ultimately allows him to be seen as a protector.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:18.497 --> 00:05:23.717
So despite Robert being forced to act with force,&nbsp;
he's still able to be accepted by the community.

00:05:24.240 --> 00:05:29.160
When Enzo first gets Robert in his care,&nbsp;
he asks if he's a good man or a bad man.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:29.160 --> 00:05:33.540
Robert replies that he doesn't know, and&nbsp;
while that answer might scare some people,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:33.540 --> 00:05:37.800
it actually comforts Enzo. In a later&nbsp;
conversation, Enzo mentions that Robert&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:37.800 --> 00:05:43.140
saying he doesn't know if he's really good or bad&nbsp;
anymore actually proves to him that he's good. He&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:43.140 --> 00:05:47.100
believes that good men don't simply proclaim&nbsp;
that they're good and that their actions speak&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:47.100 --> 00:05:52.276
far louder. This plays into a deeper aspect&nbsp;
of Robert's arc throughout the franchise.

00:05:52.276 --> 00:05:57.600
As a vigilante, Robert has always sort of walked&nbsp;
the line between good and evil. Despite there&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:57.600 --> 00:06:02.940
being good intentions behind Robert's actions,&nbsp;
he generally spares no mercy on his foes, leading&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:02.940 --> 00:06:08.160
to some horrifically bloody and brutal kills. So&nbsp;
when this "good or bad" question is posed to him,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:08.160 --> 00:06:13.537
his answer is fitting, especially given that he's&nbsp;
in sort of a personal crisis when it's asked.

00:06:13.537 --> 00:06:19.440
Robert has always resided in a sort of moral gray&nbsp;
area, but with it now being directly posed to him,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:19.440 --> 00:06:23.400
viewers get a better sense of what&nbsp;
his morality means to him. By the end,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:23.400 --> 00:06:26.280
Robert is given the fresh start&nbsp;
he felt he could never find,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:26.280 --> 00:06:31.175
which allows him to put his bad past behind&nbsp;
him and move forward as a better man.

00:06:31.560 --> 00:06:36.840
While "The Equalizer 3" is a very personal&nbsp;
look into Robert's perspective on his own&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:36.840 --> 00:06:42.060
morality and lifestyle, it also shows how&nbsp;
powerful a sense of community can be. Before&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:42.060 --> 00:06:46.680
being brought into this town, Robert was mostly&nbsp;
just a loner trying to instill his own sense of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:46.680 --> 00:06:51.600
justice onto wrongdoers. However, once Robert&nbsp;
starts getting to know the people of the town,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:51.600 --> 00:06:55.980
he sees something he hasn't seen in a long&nbsp;
time: people interacting with one another&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:55.980 --> 00:07:00.900
with genuine care and living as a community.&nbsp;
Even when Vincent does something horrible,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:00.900 --> 00:07:03.915
the people all band together&nbsp;
to help one another recover.

00:07:03.915 --> 00:07:09.300
Robert's been stuck in such a dark and violent&nbsp;
world for so long that he's almost forgotten&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:09.300 --> 00:07:14.340
that he, too, can live in a peaceful place like&nbsp;
this. It shows how meaningful being a part of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:14.340 --> 00:07:19.320
a positive-minded community can be and how a&nbsp;
kind-hearted culture can legitimately change&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:19.320 --> 00:07:24.420
someone. The good vibes of these people rub off on&nbsp;
Robert in a big way -- which is why he's willing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:24.420 --> 00:07:29.340
to put himself in harm's way to protect them.&nbsp;
Robert's experience in "The Equalizer 3" is a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:29.340 --> 00:07:34.676
reminder of how a good sense of community and&nbsp;
togetherness can warm the coldest of hearts.

00:07:35.040 --> 00:07:39.000
Within the film's depiction of community,&nbsp;
there's also a strong sense of how people&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:39.000 --> 00:07:44.160
can go from bystanders to taking a meaningful&nbsp;
part in making change happen. When Robert first&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:44.160 --> 00:07:48.540
arrives in this town, he sees that the people&nbsp;
-- while incredibly kind and genuine with one&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:48.540 --> 00:07:53.280
another -- live in fear of Vincent and his&nbsp;
men. They're often intimidated by Vincent's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:53.280 --> 00:07:58.560
violent tactics, particularly how public and&nbsp;
grisly his kills are. Even when one of their&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:58.560 --> 00:08:02.400
own is physically attacked or beaten,&nbsp;
they don't act outside of just helping&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:02.400 --> 00:08:06.840
them heal. Despite this community having&nbsp;
the numbers against Vincent and his crew,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:06.840 --> 00:08:11.676
they've been heavily outmatched by the firepower&nbsp;
and sheer viciousness of their opposition.

00:08:11.676 --> 00:08:16.440
However, as much as this community has inspired&nbsp;
Robert to have a better perspective on his life,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:16.440 --> 00:08:21.480
he has also inspired them in a way. When Robert&nbsp;
is about to sacrifice himself to keep Vincent&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:21.480 --> 00:08:25.680
from killing the townspeople, not only&nbsp;
does Enzo step in to keep Robert safe,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:25.680 --> 00:08:29.820
but the other civilians take out their&nbsp;
phones to record Vincent's actions. It's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:29.820 --> 00:08:34.260
a moment where these people step out of their&nbsp;
bystander status and take effective action&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:34.260 --> 00:08:36.600
together for the first time.
Is this really the end?

00:08:36.600 --> 00:08:41.940
Both Fuqua and Washington have stated that "The&nbsp;
Equalizer 3" ends the trilogy, and that this will&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:41.940 --> 00:08:46.800
likely be the last time these two work in this&nbsp;
franchise. In an exclusive interview with Looper,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:46.800 --> 00:08:51.016
Fuqua mentioned how sad it was to be&nbsp;
leaving "The Equalizer" franchise behind.

00:08:51.016 --> 00:08:51.900
"It's like a breakup."

00:08:51.900 --> 00:08:55.980
"There was a moment when I was sitting there&nbsp;
watching it on the big screen, and I thought, 'Oh&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:55.980 --> 00:09:01.980
man, I'm saying goodbye to Robert McCall. I don't&nbsp;
want to do that.' But everything comes to an end."

00:09:01.980 --> 00:09:05.040
In an interview with Empire,&nbsp;
Washington expressed the same&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:05.040 --> 00:09:07.800
mixed feelings about bidding&nbsp;
farewell to McCall, saying,

00:09:07.800 --> 00:09:11.160
"I don't want to give it all&nbsp;
away, but he meets someone lovely,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:11.160 --> 00:09:16.237
he's in a lovely town and he seems to be at&nbsp;
peace. That seems to be a good place to stop."

00:09:16.237 --> 00:09:21.480
Obviously, someone else can come and direct a&nbsp;
new entry or maybe a spin-off focusing on Emma,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:21.480 --> 00:09:24.420
since it seems like her story&nbsp;
is just starting. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:24.420 --> 00:09:29.100
that's probably not happening -- at least&nbsp;
for a while -- so fans can expect this to be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:29.100 --> 00:09:33.836
the last time Robert McCall will be on the big&nbsp;
screen, at least with Washington playing him.

00:09:34.140 --> 00:09:39.120
Or maybe there's a way to bring the hero of&nbsp;
the series back after all. While there hasn't&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:39.120 --> 00:09:43.620
been any talk of a sequel to "The Equalizer&nbsp;
3" to continue Robert's story, there have&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:43.620 --> 00:09:48.120
been some interesting conversations about a&nbsp;
potential prequel. In an interview with NME,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:48.120 --> 00:09:53.700
Fuqua mentioned some interest in a prequel film&nbsp;
in which Washington would return but be de-aged&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:53.700 --> 00:09:58.560
digitally. When discussing the potential of&nbsp;
de-aging AI tech, Fuqua said that he considered&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:58.560 --> 00:10:03.240
using de-aging tech in "The Equalizer 3" and&nbsp;
that he's had conversations with franchise writer&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:03.240 --> 00:10:08.638
Richard Wenk about it. De-aging AI isn't the only&nbsp;
way that Fuqua sees a prequel happening though.

00:10:08.638 --> 00:10:11.820
"That's not a conversation I've&nbsp;
ever had with Denzel. You know,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:11.820 --> 00:10:14.460
I'd have to have that conversation with&nbsp;
Denzel, and obviously, the studio."

00:10:14.460 --> 00:10:18.480
In an interview with JoBlo, Fuqua also&nbsp;
brought up potential actors to portray&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:18.480 --> 00:10:23.160
a younger Robert McCall. Fuqua mentioned that&nbsp;
he'd be interested in seeing Michael B. Jordan&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:23.160 --> 00:10:27.780
playing a younger version of Robert and was&nbsp;
a big fan of the interviewer suggesting the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:27.780 --> 00:10:31.920
name of John David Washington, Denzel's&nbsp;
son who has starred in films including&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:31.920 --> 00:10:35.460
"Tenet" and "Beckett." At the moment,&nbsp;
there's no prequel in production,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:35.460 --> 00:10:40.756
but the options are out there. It seems Fuqua is&nbsp;
willing to return for one, so it could happen.

